      "side": 1,
      "message": "This _may_ not actually work for the original intent.\n\nAFAIK, this was used on devices to turn LE Audio on when the sysprops were set to false, as the feature was \"disabled by default.\" This provided a way for developers and interested users to turn it on \"before it was ready\" and enabled by default.\n\nIf we don\u0027t enable something because the sysprop is false (or, in the new world, because all use-case sysprops that have a given framework profile as a dependency are false), then there will be no way to override that default setting on those devices.\n\nTo make it more tangible, say for example we have a Car on Android V, using an Android B prebuilt, and that car has LE Audio sysprops set to false because the feature is \"supported\" by the hardware but off by default. This option was supposed to let us/developers/OEM testers/etc. turn things on before they\u0027re on by default. With this, we can\u0027t.\n\nSince we\u0027re now breaking the \"everyone wants all roles\" assumption, the only way I can I think of to keep this functionality of \"set it to enabled when its disabled,\" while not enabling roles we don\u0027t want is to break things up per-role, or use an ENUM list on the switching mode, etc. Something that let\u0027s the educated user select the right things. It would also unfortunately let the unsuspecting user accidentally put the device in a bad state (until, for example, we start implementing LE call control). But, that could be a feature as we develop LE Call Control on cars",
